\ pow.fam — the proof of work and the header's hashes (docs/NODE.md, step 4),
\ after arith.fam, poseidon2.fam and difficulty.fam.  As tabminer's
\ miner/src/pow.rs and block.rs.
\
\ The seed file is the King James text gzipped, 1,291,059 bytes, used as it
\ is (/lib/akjv.txt.gz): read in 24-byte windows on 24-byte boundaries, the
\ last ending at the file's end, each packed three bytes to an element.  A
\ dataset item is 16 elements: a state from its index, then `parents` steps
\ each absorbing the window the state picks and permuting.  hashimoto mixes
\ 32 words from the header's hash and nonce through `accesses` reads, each
\ of two adjacent items and one window picked by a second selector, folds
\ them to 8 and compresses them with the seed.  The node computes each item
\ it needs from the file: validating a header needs the whole file.
\
\ Field values in memory are Montgomery words (arith.fam); digests given or
\ returned as canonical words say so.  Not reentrant.
\
\ powinit ( text n -- )  the seed file in memory.
\ window ( w c -- )  c (8 words) = window w.
\ item ( index c -- )  c (16 words) = dataset item index (parents: pwpar).
\ hashmix ( hh nonce mix res -- )  tabminer's hashimoto (fam's names are at
\ most 8 characters): the 8-word mix and result for the
\ header hash hh (8 words) and the 32-byte nonce, from pwitems items and
\ pwacc accesses.
\ hdr-ok ( h -- flag )  the 204-byte header's digests are canonical.
\ powhash ( h c -- ), blockid ( h c -- )  its hashes (8 words).
\ quickpow ( h t -- flag )  the result from its claimed mix meets t.
\ fullpow ( h t -- flag )  that, its mix the true one, and the result meets t.

: pwtext variable ;  : pwlen variable ;  : pwwin variable ;
: pwpar variable ;  : pwitems variable ;  : pwacc variable ;   \ the parameters (mainnet's by default)
: pwfnv variable ;                            \ the FNV prime, Montgomery
: pws variable ;  : pwmix variable ;  : pwa variable ;  : pwb variable ;  : pwx variable ;  : pwy variable ;
: pwv variable ;  : pwid variable ;  : pwhh variable ;  : pwm variable ;  : pwo variable ;
: pwh variable ;  : pwr variable ;  : pwi variable ;  : pwt variable ;
: pka variable ;  : pkn variable ;  : pkc variable ;

:M DOM_ITEM 5041 lit ;  :M DOM_SEED 5042 lit ;  :M DOM_POW 10 lit ;  :M DOM_ID 11 lit ;

: powinit  ( text n -- )
p2init dvinit
dup pwlen !  17 lit + 18 lit / pwwin !  pwtext !
1000193 lit tom pwfnv !
FE lit pwpar !  100000 lit pwitems !  40 lit pwacc !
pws @ 0= if
	40 lit alloc pws !  80 lit alloc pwmix !  40 lit alloc pwa !  40 lit alloc pwb !
	20 lit alloc pwx !  20 lit alloc pwy !  A0 lit alloc pwv !  70 lit alloc pwid !
	20 lit alloc pwhh !  20 lit alloc pwm !  20 lit alloc pwo !  20 lit alloc pwh !  20 lit alloc pwr !
then ;

: fnv  swap pwfnv @ fmul f+ ;               \ ( a b -- a*prime+b )

\ pack3 ( a n c -- )  c = the n bytes at a (n at least 1) three to an
\ element, little-endian, the last zero padded; Montgomery.
: pack3
pkc ! pkn ! pka !
pkn @ 2 lit + 3 lit / 0 lit do
	0 lit
	3 lit 0 lit do
		j 3 lit * i +  dup pkn @ u< if pka @ + c@ i 3 lit lshift lshift or else drop then
	loop
	tom pkc @ i w!
loop ;

: window  ( w c -- )
swap 18 lit *  pwlen @ 18 lit -  2dup u> if swap then drop
pwtext @ + 18 lit rot pack3 ;

\ wsel ( v -- w )  tabminer's direct_window: the bits of v below the least
\ power of two at least the windows, less the windows once if that many.
: wsel
1 lit begin dup pwwin @ u< while 1 lit lshift repeat 1 lit -  and
dup pwwin @ u< 0= if pwwin @ - then ;

: item  ( index c -- )
dup pwt !  10 lit wzero
P 2dup u< 0= if - else drop then tom pwt @ 0 lit w!
DOM_ITEM tom pwt @ 1 lit w!
pwt @ perm16
pwpar @ 0 lit do
	pwt @ 0 lit w@ fromm  pwt @ 1 lit w@ fromm
	dup 1F lit lshift rot or  swap 1 lit rshift      \ the 62-bit c0 + c1 2^31
	pwwin @ ud%  pwy @ window
	8 lit 0 lit do pwt @ i w@ pwy @ i w@ f+ pwt @ i w! loop
	pwt @ perm16
loop ;

\ pwseed ( hh nonce -- )  pws (16 words) = the seed state.
: pwseed
20 lit pwv @ pack3
pws @ 8 lit wcopy  pws @ 20 lit + 8 lit wzero  DOM_SEED tom pws @ 8 lit w!
pws @ perm16
8 lit 0 lit do pws @ i w@ pwv @ i w@ f+ pws @ i w! loop  pws @ perm16
3 lit 0 lit do pws @ i w@ pwv @ 8 lit i + w@ f+ pws @ i w! loop  pws @ perm16 ;

: hashmix  ( hh nonce mix res -- )
pwr ! pwh ! pwseed
pws @ pwmix @ 10 lit wcopy  pws @ pwmix @ 40 lit + 10 lit wcopy
pwacc @ 0 lit do
	i tom pws @ 0 lit w@ f+  pwmix @ i 1F lit and w@ fnv fromm
	pwitems @ 1 lit rshift 1 lit - and 1 lit lshift pwi !
	i tom pws @ 1 lit w@ f+  pwmix @ i 10 lit + 1F lit and w@ fnv fromm
	wsel pwx @ window
	pwi @ pwa @ item  pwi @ 1 lit + pwb @ item
	20 lit 0 lit do
		pwmix @ i w@  i 10 lit u< if pwa @ i w@ else pwb @ i 10 lit - w@ then  fnv
		pwx @ i 7 lit and w@ f+  pwmix @ i w!
	loop
loop
8 lit 0 lit do
	pwmix @ i 2 lit lshift w@  pwmix @ i 2 lit lshift 1 lit + w@ fnv
	pwmix @ i 2 lit lshift 2 lit + w@ fnv  pwmix @ i 2 lit lshift 3 lit + w@ fnv
	pwh @ i w!
loop
pwh @ pws @ pwr @ compress ;

\ ── Headers: prev_hash 0, height 32, timestamp 36, body 44, state 76,
\ aux 108, mix 140, nonce 172 ──

: dig-ok  -1 lit 8 lit 0 lit do over i w@ P u< and loop nip ;   \ ( a -- flag )  8 canonical words
: hdr-ok  dup dig-ok over 2C lit + dig-ok and over 4C lit + dig-ok and swap 8C lit + dig-ok and ;
: dtom  8 lit 0 lit do over i w@ tom over i w! loop 2drop ;     \ ( a c -- )  8 canonical words in
: dfrom  8 lit 0 lit do dup i w@ fromm over i w! loop drop ;    \ ( a -- )  8 words out, in place

: powhash  ( h c -- )
swap
DOM_POW tom pwv @ 0 lit w!
dup pwv @ 4 lit + dtom
dup 20 lit + @ P 2dup u< 0= if - else drop then tom pwv @ 9 lit w!
dup 24 lit + @ 3FFFFFFF lit and tom pwv @ A lit w!
dup 24 lit + @ 1E lit rshift over 28 lit + @ 2 lit lshift or 3FFFFFFF lit and tom pwv @ B lit w!
dup 28 lit + @ 1C lit rshift tom pwv @ C lit w!
dup 2C lit + pwv @ 34 lit + dtom
dup 4C lit + pwv @ 54 lit + dtom
6C lit + 20 lit pwv @ 74 lit + pack3
pwv @ 28 lit rot hash ;

: blockid  ( h c -- )
swap
DOM_ID tom pwid @ 0 lit w!
dup pwid @ 4 lit + powhash
dup 8C lit + pwid @ 24 lit + dtom
AC lit + 20 lit pwid @ 44 lit + pack3
pwid @ 1C lit rot hash ;

\ quickpow ( h t -- flag )  the result from the header's claimed mix meets t.
: quickpow
over pwhh @ powhash
over 8C lit + pwm @ dtom
pwhh @ rot AC lit + pwseed
pwm @ pws @ pwo @ compress  pwo @ dfrom
pwo @ swap meets ;

\ fullpow ( h t -- flag )  quickpow, and the true mix the claimed one and its
\ result meeting t.
: fullpow
2dup quickpow if
	over pwhh @ powhash
	pwhh @ 2 lit pick AC lit + pwo @ pwr @ hashmix
	pwo @ dfrom  pwr @ dfrom
	pwo @ rot 8C lit + 8 lit wcmp 0=
	pwr @ rot meets and
else 2drop 0 lit then ;
